  "section_notes": "The final S2 keeps the 55 °C test and gives customers per-model numeric failure rates without public disclosure, but exceeding 5% only triggers corrective action, so the flagship can keep selling (favouring Northwind). S5 sets a permanent, automatic mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 with no interim window, which bites Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9. S4 (36 months) and S3 (6-year retrofit) sit inside the acceptable ranges and favour the respective companies."
